From 5b1cc3069785d67d5d86b5215095fe4c4146513a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: drabikp <drabik.p@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 11:06:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] DigitalAppWidget: size the clock from the host's real
 bounds

On a multi-display device the digital clock widget renders at the wrong size,
badly enough to be unreadable or clipped. It is an AOSP bug, not a device one,
and it hits any foldable or any phone with a cover panel.

relayoutWidget() sized the clock from OPTION_APPWIDGET_MIN_WIDTH/HEIGHT and
OPTION_APPWIDGET_MAX_WIDTH/HEIGHT. Those four are an AGGREGATE: when a widget
can appear on more than one display profile, the launcher reports the minimum
of the minima and the maximum of the maxima across ALL profiles. On a device
whose two panels differ substantially the resulting box matches neither, so
the clock is laid out for a display it is not on.

Use OPTION_APPWIDGET_SIZES instead. That is the per-profile list the host
actually publishes, and RemoteViews can carry one sized view per entry, so the
host picks the one matching its real bounds at draw time. Capped at 16 entries
to match RemoteViews.MAX_INIT_VIEW_COUNT, which throws above that.

Two smaller fixes come with it. A last-resort 40dp fallback is used when the
host supplies no size at all AND the provider info cannot be read -- without it
the widget is laid out for a 0x0 box and the font collapses to 1px. And
widgetFeatures="configuration_optional" is set, so the widget can be placed
from a default_workspace without the configuration activity blocking it.

Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5
Change-Id: I020282f08c646403eaaedc5dad401ca1b9f6b03a
